{"title":"Career Roadmap · Obstetric Ultrasound Technician","role":"Obstetric Ultrasound Technician","summary":"An Obstetric Ultrasound Technician supports ultrasound imaging of pregnancy, including assessment of fetal development, fetal anatomy, maternal pelvic structures and pregnancy-related conditions.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An Obstetric Ultrasound Technician supports ultrasound imaging of pregnancy, including assessment of fetal development, fetal anatomy, maternal pelvic structures and pregnancy-related conditions."},{"type":"h","text":"The role typically involves:"},{"type":"h","text":"Preparing patients for ultrasound examinations"},{"type":"h","text":"Obtaining relevant clinical history"},{"type":"h","text":"Positioning patients appropriately"},{"type":"h","text":"Operating ultrasound equipment"},{"type":"h","text":"Selecting appropriate probes and imaging settings"},{"type":"h","text":"Acquiring diagnostic-quality images"},{"type":"h","text":"Performing standardized measurements within authorized scope"},{"type":"h","text":"Maintaining patient comfort and privacy"},{"type":"h","text":"Documenting examination information"},{"type":"h","text":"Maintaining equipment and infection-control standards"},{"type":"h","text":"Supporting radiologists, obstetricians or other authorized clinicians"},{"type":"note","label":"Important scope note","text":"In India, ultrasound practice is subject to professional qualification requirements and the PCPNDT regulatory framework. An ultrasound technician/technologist should not be represented as an independent diagnostician. Final interpretation and diagnostic reporting are generally the responsibility of an appropriately qualified and authorized medical practitioner. Exact eligibility and permitted duties depend on the candidate's recognized qualification, institution and applicable regulations."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Direction"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Sonography education + supervised clinical training"}],[{"text":"2030–2034"},{"text":"Junior Ultrasound / Sonography Technologist"}],[{"text":"2034–2040"},{"text":"Obstetric Sonography Technologist / Senior Sonographer"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Senior Technologist / Ultrasound Unit Coordinator / Clinical Educator"}]]}]},{"heading":"Anatomy & Physiology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Build strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Female reproductive anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Uterus"},{"type":"h","text":"Cervix"},{"type":"h","text":"Endometrium"},{"type":"h","text":"Ovaries"},{"type":"h","text":"Fallopian tubes"},{"type":"h","text":"Pelvic structures"},{"type":"h","text":"Pregnancy physiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Embryonic development"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal development"},{"type":"h","text":"Placental development"},{"type":"h","text":"Amniotic fluid"},{"type":"h","text":"Umbilical cord"},{"type":"h","text":"Maternal physiological changes"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal anatomy"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand the basic sonographic appearance of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Head"},{"type":"h","text":"Brain"},{"type":"h","text":"Face"},{"type":"h","text":"Spine"},{"type":"h","text":"Chest"},{"type":"h","text":"Heart"},{"type":"h","text":"Abdomen"},{"type":"h","text":"Kidneys"},{"type":"h","text":"Bladder"},{"type":"h","text":"Limbs"}]},{"heading":"Ultrasound Physics","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Ultrasound physics is fundamental to becoming a competent sonographer."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"h","text":"Sound waves"},{"type":"h","text":"Frequency"},{"type":"h","text":"Wavelength"},{"type":"h","text":"Amplitude"},{"type":"h","text":"Acoustic impedance"},{"type":"h","text":"Reflection"},{"type":"h","text":"Refraction"},{"type":"h","text":"Scattering"},{"type":"h","text":"Absorption"},{"type":"h","text":"Attenuation"},{"type":"h","text":"Resolution"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler principles"},{"type":"h","text":"Image quality"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Axial resolution"},{"type":"h","text":"Lateral resolution"},{"type":"h","text":"Contrast resolution"},{"type":"h","text":"Depth"},{"type":"h","text":"Gain"},{"type":"h","text":"Time-gain compensation"},{"type":"h","text":"Dynamic range"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus"},{"type":"h","text":"Depth settings"}]},{"heading":"Ultrasound Equipment","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Become familiar with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound console"},{"type":"h","text":"Transducers"},{"type":"h","text":"Curvilinear probes"},{"type":"h","text":"Linear probes"},{"type":"h","text":"Phased-array probes"},{"type":"h","text":"Transvaginal probes"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler systems"},{"type":"h","text":"Color Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"Power Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"3D ultrasound"},{"type":"h","text":"4D ultrasound"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand the relationship between:"},{"type":"flow","items":["transducer","frequency","penetration","resolution","clinical application"]}]},{"heading":"Obstetric Ultrasound","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Build knowledge of examinations across pregnancy."},{"type":"h","text":"Early pregnancy"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn the imaging principles associated with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Gestational sac"},{"type":"h","text":"Yolk sac"},{"type":"h","text":"Embryo"},{"type":"h","text":"Cardiac activity"},{"type":"h","text":"Crown-rump length"},{"type":"h","text":"Pregnancy location"},{"type":"h","text":"Early pregnancy assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Second trimester"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop familiarity with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal biometry"},{"type":"h","text":"Anatomy survey"},{"type":"h","text":"Placenta"},{"type":"h","text":"Amniotic fluid"},{"type":"h","text":"Cervix"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal position"},{"type":"h","text":"Third trimester"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Growth assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal biometry"},{"type":"h","text":"Placental location"},{"type":"h","text":"Amniotic fluid"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal presentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler studies"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal well-being assessment"}]},{"heading":"Fetal Biometry","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Learn the principles behind measurements such as:"},{"type":"h","text":"Biparietal diameter (BPD)"},{"type":"h","text":"Head circumference (HC)"},{"type":"h","text":"Abdominal circumference (AC)"},{"type":"h","text":"Femur length (FL)"},{"type":"h","text":"Crown-rump length (CRL)"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand that accurate measurement requires:"},{"type":"h","text":"Correct anatomical plane"},{"type":"h","text":"Correct caliper placement"},{"type":"h","text":"Proper image optimization"},{"type":"h","text":"Consistent technique"},{"type":"h","text":"Appropriate gestational-age context"}]},{"heading":"Doppler Ultrasound","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Build foundational knowledge of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Color Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"Spectral Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"Pulsed-wave Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler angle"},{"type":"h","text":"Velocity"},{"type":"h","text":"Resistance index"},{"type":"h","text":"Pulsatility index"},{"type":"h","text":"Flow patterns"},{"type":"p","text":"In obstetric applications, develop awareness of Doppler assessment involving structures such as:"},{"type":"h","text":"Umbilical artery"},{"type":"h","text":"Middle cerebral artery"},{"type":"h","text":"Uterine arteries"},{"type":"h","text":"Ductus venosus in appropriate clinical contexts"},{"type":"p","text":"Advanced interpretation should remain within the role and supervision permitted by the individual's qualification."}]},{"heading":"Patient Care & Communication","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Pregnancy imaging can be emotionally sensitive."},{"type":"h","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional communication"},{"type":"h","text":"Privacy awareness"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"Consent-related workflow awareness"},{"type":"h","text":"Respectful communication"},{"type":"h","text":"Cultural sensitivity"},{"type":"h","text":"Anxiety management"},{"type":"h","text":"Confidentiality"},{"type":"h","text":"Chaperone/professional-boundary awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"A good ultrasound technician should be technically accurate and patient-centred."},{"type":"h","text":"Year-by-Year Development"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"h","text":"Anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Physiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical terminology"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic physics"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient care"},{"type":"h","text":"Infection control"},{"type":"h","text":"Build"},{"type":"h","text":"Anatomy revision portfolio"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound terminology database"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic image-identification exercises"},{"type":"h","text":"Excel fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Sonography Core"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound physics"},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment"},{"type":"h","text":"Transducer selection"},{"type":"h","text":"Image optimization"},{"type":"h","text":"Abdominal ultrasound"},{"type":"h","text":"Pelvic ultrasound"},{"type":"h","text":"Obstetric fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Practical exposure"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn supervised:"},{"type":"h","text":"Probe handling"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic scanning planes"},{"type":"h","text":"Image optimization"},{"type":"h","text":"Measurement techniques"},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Obstetric Specialization"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"h","text":"First-trimester scanning"},{"type":"h","text":"Second-trimester anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Third-trimester assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal biometry"},{"type":"h","text":"Placental assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"3D/4D ultrasound"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Prioritize exposure to:"},{"type":"h","text":"Obstetrics departments"},{"type":"h","text":"Maternal-fetal medicine"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiology departments"},{"type":"h","text":"Diagnostic imaging centres"},{"type":"h","text":"Hospitals with high-volume ultrasound services"},{"type":"h","text":"Core Technical Skill Stack"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound physics"},{"type":"h","text":"Probe selection"},{"type":"h","text":"Image optimization"},{"type":"h","text":"B-mode imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"3D/4D imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Obstetrics"},{"type":"h","text":"Pregnancy anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal biometry"},{"type":"h","text":"Placental assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Amniotic fluid assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Gestational-age concepts"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"Examination preparation"},{"type":"h","text":"Image acquisition"},{"type":"h","text":"Documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Infection control"},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"PACS"},{"type":"h","text":"DICOM"},{"type":"h","text":"RIS"},{"type":"h","text":"Digital image storage"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound workstation"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic data analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Workflow"},{"type":"h","text":"Referral / Examination Request"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Identification"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical History & Preparation"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"Appropriate Transducer Selection"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound Examination"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Optimization"},{"type":"h","text":"Required Measurements / Image Acquisition"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler / Additional Imaging When Indicated"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Storage & Documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinician / Radiologist Review"},{"type":"h","text":"Final Diagnostic Interpretation & Report"},{"type":"p","text":"The technician's role is primarily image acquisition and technical support within the authorized scope; it should not be represented as independent diagnostic reporting."},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Projects"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Fetal Biometry Learning Tool"},{"type":"p","text":"Create an educational application demonstrating:"},{"type":"h","text":"BPD"},{"type":"h","text":"HC"},{"type":"h","text":"AC"},{"type":"h","text":"FL"},{"type":"h","text":"CRL"},{"type":"p","text":"The application can use synthetic measurements to demonstrate how measurements are recorded and organized."},{"type":"note","label":"Tools","text":"Python / Excel / JavaScript."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Ultrasound Image Quality Dashboard"},{"type":"h","text":"Create a simulated dataset containing:"},{"type":"h","text":"Examination type"},{"type":"h","text":"Transducer type"},{"type":"h","text":"Image-quality score"},{"type":"h","text":"Examination duration"},{"type":"h","text":"Repeat-scan frequency"},{"type":"h","text":"Technical issue category"},{"type":"h","text":"Visualize the data using:"},{"type":"p","text":"Power BI / Excel."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Ultrasound Equipment Maintenance Tracker"},{"type":"h","text":"Track:"},{"type":"h","text":"Machine ID"},{"type":"h","text":"Probe ID"},{"type":"h","text":"Maintenance date"},{"type":"h","text":"Calibration/service date"},{"type":"h","text":"Fault category"},{"type":"h","text":"Downtime"},{"type":"h","text":"Next service date"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Obstetric Examination Workflow System"},{"type":"h","text":"Create a digital workflow showing:"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Registration"},{"type":"h","text":"Examination Request"},{"type":"h","text":"Pregnancy Details"},{"type":"h","text":"Scan Type"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Acquisition"},{"type":"h","text":"Measurements"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Storage"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiologist / Clinician Review"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Doppler Education Dashboard"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop an educational visualization for:"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler waveform concepts"},{"type":"h","text":"Velocity"},{"type":"h","text":"RI"},{"type":"h","text":"PI"},{"type":"h","text":"Flow patterns"},{"type":"p","text":"Use simulated data rather than real patient records."}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Priority settings"},{"type":"h","text":"Maternal-fetal medicine departments"},{"type":"h","text":"Obstetric ultrasound units"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiology departments"},{"type":"h","text":"Diagnostic imaging centres"},{"type":"h","text":"Large multispecialty hospitals"},{"type":"h","text":"Women's hospitals"},{"type":"h","text":"Internship progression"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound Department Orientation"},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment & Probe Training"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic Image Acquisition"},{"type":"h","text":"Obstetric Scanning Observation"},{"type":"h","text":"Supervised Measurements"},{"type":"h","text":"Supervised Examination Workflow"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Competency Assessment"}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Depending on recognized qualification and employer requirements:"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Sonography Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Sonography Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Obstetric Sonography Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound Technician"},{"type":"h","text":"Diagnostic Imaging Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Sonography Assistant"},{"type":"p","text":"The most appropriate initial positioning is generally:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Recognized Medical Sonography/Ultrasound Technology qualification","clinical internship","Ultrasound/Sonography Technologist","Obstetric specialization"]},{"type":"h","text":"Employer Skill Matrix"},{"type":"table","header":["Employer Requirement","Candidate Should Demonstrate"],"rows":[[{"text":"Ultrasound operation"},{"text":"Confident equipment handling"}],[{"text":"Image acquisition"},{"text":"Consistent diagnostic-quality images"}],[{"text":"Obstetric scanning"},{"text":"Knowledge of pregnancy imaging"}],[{"text":"Fetal biometry"},{"text":"Accurate supervised measurements"}],[{"text":"Doppler"},{"text":"Basic Doppler operation"}],[{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"Professional communication"}],[{"text":"Infection control"},{"text":"Appropriate cleaning and hygiene"}],[{"text":"Documentation"},{"text":"Accurate examination records"}],[{"text":"PACS"},{"text":"Digital image management"}],[{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Appropriate ultrasound and clinical safety practices"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Useful supporting training includes:"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic Life Support (BLS)"},{"type":"h","text":"Infection prevention"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient safety"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical terminology"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound physics"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"PACS/DICOM fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Excel"},{"type":"h","text":"Power BI"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare data analytics"},{"type":"p","text":"For clinical sonography, formal recognized education and supervised scanning experience are substantially more important than generic online certificates."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Possible postgraduate directions include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Medical Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Sonography-related postgraduate programs"},{"type":"h","text":"Diagnostic Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiology Technology-related programs"},{"type":"h","text":"Maternal & Fetal Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced obstetric imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Maternal-fetal imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"Management"},{"type":"h","text":"Hospital Administration"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Management"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Quality"},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Health Informatics"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical Imaging Informatics"},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Analytics"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical AI"},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"h","text":"1. Obstetric Sonography"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"h","text":"Pregnancy imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal biometry"},{"type":"h","text":"Anatomy surveys"},{"type":"h","text":"Placental assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"2. Maternal-Fetal Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop advanced exposure to:"},{"type":"h","text":"High-risk pregnancy imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced fetal imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"3. Gynecological Sonography"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"h","text":"Uterus"},{"type":"h","text":"Endometrium"},{"type":"h","text":"Ovaries"},{"type":"h","text":"Pelvic pathology imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"4. 3D/4D Sonography"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop expertise in:"},{"type":"h","text":"3D reconstruction"},{"type":"h","text":"4D imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Surface rendering"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced visualization"},{"type":"h","text":"5. Doppler Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"h","text":"Vascular flow"},{"type":"h","text":"Obstetric Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"Hemodynamic assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"6. Ultrasound Application Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Work with medical-device companies in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound system demonstrations"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical applications"},{"type":"h","text":"User training"},{"type":"h","text":"Product support"},{"type":"h","text":"Emerging Technologies"},{"type":"h","text":"AI-Assisted Ultrasound"},{"type":"h","text":"AI can increasingly assist with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Image optimization"},{"type":"h","text":"Anatomical identification"},{"type":"h","text":"Standardized measurements"},{"type":"h","text":"Image quality assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Workflow assistance"},{"type":"p","text":"AI should be viewed as clinical decision support, not a replacement for qualified clinical interpretation."},{"type":"h","text":"Automated Fetal Biometry"},{"type":"h","text":"Future systems can assist with:"},{"type":"h","text":"Automatic anatomical plane detection"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal measurements"},{"type":"h","text":"Growth assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Measurement consistency"},{"type":"h","text":"3D/4D Imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"Advanced ultrasound is increasingly incorporating:"},{"type":"h","text":"3D reconstruction"},{"type":"h","text":"4D real-time imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Automated volume analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Improved fetal visualization"},{"type":"h","text":"Portable Ultrasound"},{"type":"p","text":"Handheld ultrasound systems are expanding access to point-of-care imaging."},{"type":"h","text":"Future sonographers should understand:"},{"type":"h","text":"Portable systems"},{"type":"h","text":"Wireless probes"},{"type":"h","text":"Cloud-connected imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Remote consultation workflows"}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Recognized Sonography / Ultrasound Technology Qualification"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior Ultrasound Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound / Sonography Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Obstetric Sonography Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Sonographer"},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Imaging Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound Unit Lead / Coordinator"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Educator / Applications Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the candidate should have:"},{"type":"h","text":"Medical"},{"type":"h","text":"Female reproductive anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Pregnancy physiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Basic pathology"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound physics"},{"type":"h","text":"B-mode"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"Probe selection"},{"type":"h","text":"Image optimization"},{"type":"h","text":"3D/4D fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Obstetric"},{"type":"h","text":"Pregnancy scanning workflow"},{"type":"h","text":"Fetal biometry"},{"type":"h","text":"Placental assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Amniotic fluid assessment"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler fundamentals"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"Image acquisition"},{"type":"h","text":"Documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Infection control"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient communication"},{"type":"h","text":"Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"PACS"},{"type":"h","text":"DICOM"},{"type":"h","text":"RIS"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound workstation"},{"type":"h","text":"Excel"},{"type":"h","text":"Power BI"},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"h","text":"Attention to detail"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient privacy"},{"type":"h","text":"Empathy"},{"type":"h","text":"Communication"},{"type":"h","text":"Protocol adherence"},{"type":"h","text":"Safety awareness"},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate should be able to demonstrate:"},{"type":"p","text":"“I have formal Medical Sonography/Ultrasound Technology training, supervised clinical experience in obstetric ultrasound, competency in ultrasound equipment and image acquisition, knowledge of fetal biometry and Doppler fundamentals, and strong patient-care, documentation and safety skills.”"},{"type":"h","text":"Database Note"},{"type":"p","text":"The target “Obstetric Ultrasound Technician” is a reasonable specialization, but the database should distinguish the technical imaging role from the medical diagnostic role."},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended hierarchy:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Medical Sonography / Ultrasound Technology","Ultrasound/Sonography Technologist","Obstetric Sonography Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"rather than implying that a generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT graduate can independently perform or interpret obstetric ultrasound examinations."},{"type":"p","text":"For India, the database should also retain a PCPNDT/professional eligibility caveat, because ultrasound services involving prenatal imaging operate within specific regulatory requirements."}]}]}